  "Question": "The conjugate of \\(1+i\\) is \\(1-i\\). What is their product?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The product of \\(z\\) and its conjugate equals the square of its modulus, which is \\(2\\) here.\n\nAlternative method 1: Difference of squares\n\nThe factors have the same real term and opposite imaginary terms, so the difference-of-squares formula applies. Since \\(i^2=-1\\),\n\\[\n(1+i)(1-i)=1-i^2=2.\n\\]",
